{"name":"Coffee Liqueur","hex":"#6a513b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"coffee liqueur","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A liqueur with coffee, such as Tia Maria or Kahlua"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/coffee_liqueur"}],"entries":[{"title":"List of liqueur brands","blocks":[{"text":"Liqueurs are alcoholic beverages that are bottled with added sugar and have added flavours that are usually derived from fruits, herbs, or nuts. Liqueurs are distinct from eaux-de-vie, fruit brandy, and flavored liquors, which contain no added sugar. Most liqueurs range between 15% and 55% alcohol by volume."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/ManyAmari.jpg/330px-ManyAmari.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_liqueur_brands"},{"title":"Coffee","blocks":[{"text":"Coffee is a beverage brewed from roasted, ground coffee beans. Dark-colored and bitter, coffee has a stimulating effect on humans due to its caffeine content; however decaffeinated coffee is also commercially available. There are also various coffee substitutes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Latte_and_dark_coffee.jpg/330px-Latte_and_dark_coffee.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coffee"},{"title":"Liqueur","blocks":[{"text":"A liqueur or cordial is an alcoholic drink composed of spirits and additional flavorings such as sugar, fruits, herbs, and spices. Often served with or after dessert, they are typically heavily sweetened and un-aged, beyond a resting period during production, when necessary, for their flavors to mingle."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/92/Licor-Beir%C3%A3o-%26-Orus_-_Orus_Clothing_%28cropped%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Liqueur"},{"title":"Coffee (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Coffee is a brownish color that is a representation of a roasted coffee bean. Different types of coffee beans have different colors when roasted—the color coffee represents an average."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Roasted_coffee_beans.jpg/330px-Roasted_coffee_beans.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coffee_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Sombai_Liqueur_Anise_%26_Coffee.jpg/500px-Sombai_Liqueur_Anise_%26_Coffee.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Sombai_Liqueur_Anise_%26_Coffee.jpg/1280px-Sombai_Liqueur_Anise_%26_Coffee.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Sombai_Liqueur_Anise_%26_Coffee.jpg/500px-Sombai_Liqueur_Anise_%26_Coffee.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Bottles of Sombai Anise & Coffee rice liqueur","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASombai_Liqueur_Anise_%26_Coffee.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Carolans.jpg/500px-Carolans.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Carolans.jpg/500px-Carolans.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A bottle and glass of Carolans","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACarolans.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Creme_de_Cassis.jpg/330px-Creme_de_Cassis.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Creme_de_Cassis.j